# Two-minute offline development walkthrough — not yet rehearsed

After an authorized environment and runtime validation, invoke
`python scripts/demo.py --offline --out report/demo.html` with a fresh destination,
then open the local HTML file. This document describes the intended journey;
construction has not produced a measured or rehearsed demo artifact.

0:00–0:20: state the four classes, one-message schema and fictional development scope.
The public fixture may be inspected as explicitly public raw development source.

0:20–0:50: inspect approved transformed development cards. The documented `dev-008`
uncued NAME miss becomes an output-suppressed card. Its leak remains in regex metrics.
No raw missed value appears in the report, exception, card or diagnostics.

0:50–1:20: compare coverage, exact per-class quality, normal/challenge slices and
residual/overredaction numerators. Frontier/base/finetuned are unmeasured. Missing
metrics and intervals remain null; cost and controlled timing are unavailable.

1:20–1:45: distinguish the training-plan validator from an actual training receipt,
and the declared-ancestry auditor from independent test custody. No real trained
model, sealed test or resource measurement is supplied.

1:45–2:00: show limitations and the open decision. A negative future result is valid;
there is currently no evidence that fine-tuning earns adoption.

The later full experiment needs all four actually executed arms, independently
audited held-out families, real licensed training lineage, costs and uncertainty.
Those obligations cannot be substituted by this development walkthrough.
